    {
      "block_id": "2605.25334_p4_b30",
      "text": "Figure 2: The overall architecture of the proposed GAMSI. It consists of two key modules: (1)\nMetric-Structure Decoupled Queries (MSDQ): routes two sets of learnable queries into independent\npathways via a task-decoupled attention mask, separately encoding metric-depth and 3D structural\ncues. (2) Expert-Guided Visual Grounding (EVG): anchors each pathway to the feature space of a\ncomplementary visual expert (Depth Anything and VGGT), injecting task-specific priors for reliable\nspatial understanding.\n",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        285.18,
        504.67,
        349.76
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        432,
        1140,
        2018,
        1399
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 10.06,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 504,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25334_p4_b31",
      "text": "3\nMethodology\n",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        358.51,
        193.01,
        370.46
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        432,
        1434,
        772,
        1481
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 11.96,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Medi",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 13,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25334_p4_b32",
      "text": "As illustrated in Figure 2, GAMSI jointly learns 3D structural and metric-depth representations from\nimage\u2013text inputs through two tightly coupled designs. The first is Metric-Structure Decoupled\nQueries (MSDQ), a dual-pathway query mechanism that employs task-decoupled attention to inde-\npendently encode geometry-level structural cues and scale-aware metric-depth cues, while a shared\nself-attention backbone preserves cross-pathway interaction. The second is Expert-Guided Visual\nGrounding (EVG), which anchors each pathway\u2019s queries in the feature spaces of complementary\nvisual experts, namely a 3D reconstruction model for structural grounding and a metric depth esti-\nmator for scale grounding, thereby injecting pathway-specific priors. Built upon a general MLLM\nbackbone, GAMSI is trained in two stages: spatial perception alignment, followed by multi-task\nspatial understanding fine-tuning.\n",
      "bbox": [
        107.64,
        384.04,
        505.65,
        492.14
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        430,
        1536,
        2022,
        1968
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.9,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 901,
      "block_type": 0
    },
